    q: 'What does DDP shipping from China to the UAE include?',
    a: 'A true DDP quote must include 6 cost blocks — China export clearance, freight, UAE clearance, duty, VAT and last-mile — with scope varying by forwarder. In practice scope varies between forwarders, so confirm in writing whether destination THC, customs handling, demurrage/detention and cargo insurance are included before you compare prices.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who pays UAE import duty and VAT under DDP?',
    a: 'The seller pays both lines: 5% VAT on CIF+duty plus 5% duty on CIF, a ×1.1025 stack. The forwarder normally settles these on the seller’s behalf during UAE clearance.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the difference between DDP, DDU/DAP and EXW/FOB?',
    a: 'DDP is the maximum-seller term: 1 party clears export, pays freight, clears UAE import and pays the ×1.1025 stack; DAP leaves import clearance/taxes to the buyer. EXW and FOB give the buyer much more responsibility, from picking up at the seller’s premises (EXW) or taking over once goods are on board (FOB).',
